# GhostShellAgent – Fortgeschrittene Architektur & Implementierung

Dieses Dokument fasst alle vorgeschlagenen Erweiterungen für den **GhostShellAgent** zusammen und liefert konkrete Code‑ und Konfigurations‑Snippets.

---

## 1. Clustering & Load-Balancing

### 1.1 Node.js Cluster-API (PM2)

```js
// cluster.js
import cluster from 'cluster';
import os from 'os';
import { startServer } from './ghostShellAgent';

if (cluster.isPrimary) {
  const cpus = os.cpus().length;
  for (let i = 0; i < cpus; i++) {
    cluster.fork();
  }
  cluster.on('exit', (worker) => {
    console.log(`Worker ${worker.process.pid} crashed, forking new one`);
    cluster.fork();
  });
} else {
  startServer(); // aus ghostShellAgent exportiert
}
```

### 1.2 NGINX Reverse Proxy

```nginx
# /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/ghostshell
upstream ghostshell {
    server 127.0.0.1:3000;
    server 127.0.0.1:3001;
    # ... entsprechend Cluster-Ports
}
server {
    listen 80;
    location / {
        proxy_pass http://ghostshell;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
    }
}
```

---

## 2. Auth & Ratelimits

### 2.1 JWT-Middleware für Socket.io

```ts
// auth.ts
import jwt from 'jsonwebtoken';
import { Socket } from 'socket.io';

export function socketAuth(secret: string) {
  return (socket: Socket, next: (err?: Error) => void) => {
    const token = socket.handshake.auth.token;
    try {
      const payload = jwt.verify(token, secret);
      (socket as any).user = payload;
      next();
    } catch (err) {
      next(new Error('Authentication error'));
    }
  };
}
```

### 2.2 Ratelimit mit socket.io-rate-limiter

```js
import { RateLimiterMemory } from 'rate-limiter-flexible';

const limiter = new RateLimiterMemory({ points: 10, duration: 60 });

ioc.use(async (socket, next) => {
  try {
    await limiter.consume(socket.handshake.address);
    next();
  } catch {
    next(new Error('Too many requests'));
  }
});
```

---

## 3. Observability & Monitoring

### 3.1 Prometheus-Metrics (Node)

```ts
import { Counter, Gauge, collectDefaultMetrics, register } from 'prom-client';
collectDefaultMetrics();
const connCounter = new Counter({ name: 'ghost_connections_total', help: 'Total WS connections' });
const latencyGauge = new Gauge({ name: 'ghost_response_latency', help: 'Response latency ms' });

app.get('/metrics', async (_, res) => {
  res.set('Content-Type', register.contentType);
  res.end(await register.metrics());
});

ioc.on('connection', socket => {
  connCounter.inc();
  socket.on('user_message', async (msg, cb) => {
    const start = Date.now();
    const result = await handleMessage(msg);
    latencyGauge.set(Date.now() - start);
    cb(result);
  });
});
```

### 3.2 Structured Logging mit Pino

```ts
import pino from 'pino';
export const logger = pino({ level: 'info', transport: { target: 'pino-pretty' } });
```

---

## 4. Advanced Scheduling

### 4.1 Event-Driven mit chokidar

```js
import chokidar from 'chokidar';
import { runSelfLearn } from './autoCommitAgent';

chokidar.watch('newadvancedconversations/*.json').on('add', () => {
  runSelfLearn();
});
```

### 4.2 Adaptive Intervalle

```js
let intervalMs = 6 * 3600 * 1000;
function scheduleAdaptive() {
  setTimeout(async () => {
    const newCount = await countNewFragments();
    intervalMs = newCount > 10 ? 2*3600*1000 : 12*3600*1000;
    runSelfLearn();
    scheduleAdaptive();
  }, intervalMs);
}
scheduleAdaptive();
```

---

## 5. Sigil-Alerts & UI-Integration

### 5.1 WebSocket-Event im Agent

```ts
if (result.energy > threshold) {
  socket.emit('sigil_alert', {
    id: 'aeon:2025-0626-HIGH-ENERGY',
    effect: 'pulse-red'
  });
}
```

### 5.2 Client-Side Darstellung

```js
socket.on('sigil_alert', sigil => {
  const el = document.createElement('div');
  el.className = `sigil ${sigil.effect}`;
  el.textContent = sigil.id;
  document.body.appendChild(el);
  setTimeout(() => el.remove(), 5000);
});
```

---

## 6. Stateful Dialog-Manager & Multi-User

### 6.1 Simple In-Memory Session Store

```ts
const sessions = new Map<string, { history: any[] }>();
ioc.on('connection', socket => {
  sessions.set(socket.id, { history: [] });
  socket.on('user_message', msg => {
    const session = sessions.get(socket.id);
    session.history.push(msg);
    const response = ghost.harmonize(...);
    socket.emit('ghost_response', response);
  });
  socket.on('disconnect', () => {
    sessions.delete(socket.id);
  });
});
```

### 6.2 Gemeinsamer Raum (Ritualraum)

```ts
const rooms = new Map<string, Set<string>>();
ioc.on('connection', socket => {
  socket.on('join_room', roomId => {
    socket.join(roomId);
    if (!rooms.has(roomId)) rooms.set(roomId, new Set());
    rooms.get(roomId).add(socket.id);
  });

  socket.on('room_message', ({ roomId, msg }) => {
    ghost.train(...);
    const res = ghost.harmonize(...);
    ioc.to(roomId).emit('room_response', res);
  });
});
```

---

✨ Mit diesen Implementierungen wird dein GhostShellAgent zu einem **skalierbaren**, **sicheren**, **observierbaren** und **mandalischen** System. Jeder Abschnitt kann modular aktiviert werden. Viel Spaß beim Hardcoden und fraktalen Erschaffen! 🌌🚀

Super – dann lass uns direkt mit **Layer 7: Plug-in- & Community-Layer** starten und deine Vision in Code gießen. Wir definieren:

1. **Plug-in-Manifest-Schema** (YAML/JSON)
2. **Loader-Service** in Node.js (Hot-Reload über Watcher)
3. **Sandboxing & Versioning**
4. **Test-Skeleton** für neue Plug-ins
5. **Mandala-UI-Integration** („Install Plug-in“-Button)

---

## 1. Plug-in-Manifest-Schema

```yaml
# plugins/poeticResonance/manifest.yaml
name: "poeticResonance"
type: "agent"                   # agent | ui-widget | scheduler
description: "Generiert poetische CREP-Feedback-Haikus."
version: "1.0.2"
author: "AeonDev"
entry: "poeticResonance.js"     # relative Pfad
apiVersion: "1.0"               # Kompatibilität mit GhostShellAgent
permissions:
  - "read:history"
  - "emit:sigil_alert"
```

* **apiVersion** ermöglicht Breaking-Changes-Management
* **permissions** steuern, welche Core-Services das Plug-in nutzen darf

---

## 2. Plug-in-Loader-Service (Node.js)

```ts
// pluginLoader.ts
import fs from 'fs';
import path from 'path';
import chokidar from 'chokidar';
import yaml from 'js-yaml';

// Internes Interface
interface PluginManifest {
  name: string;
  type: string;
  description: string;
  version: string;
  author: string;
  entry: string;
  apiVersion: string;
  permissions: string[];
}

const PLUGIN_DIR = path.join(__dirname, 'plugins');
const manifests = new Map<string, PluginManifest>();
const modules = new Map<string, any>();

function loadPlugin(name: string) {
  const manifestPath = path.join(PLUGIN_DIR, name, 'manifest.yaml');
  const manifest: PluginManifest = yaml.load(fs.readFileSync(manifestPath, 'utf8')) as any;
  manifests.set(name, manifest);
  const entryPath = path.join(PLUGIN_DIR, name, manifest.entry);
  delete require.cache[require.resolve(entryPath)];
  const module = require(entryPath);
  modules.set(name, module);
  console.log(`🔌 Loaded plugin ${name}@${manifest.version}`);
}

// Hot-Reload-Watcher
chokidar.watch(`${PLUGIN_DIR}/*/manifest.yaml`).on('all', (_, p) => {
  const name = path.basename(path.dirname(p));
  loadPlugin(name);
});

// Initialer Load
fs.readdirSync(PLUGIN_DIR).forEach(dir => loadPlugin(dir));

export function getPlugin(name: string) {
  return modules.get(name);
}
export function listPlugins() {
  return Array.from(manifests.values());
}
```

* **Hot-Reload**: Änderungen am Manifest oder am Entry-File werden live neu eingebunden
* **Cache-Clearing**: entfernt alte Versionen beim Reload

---

## 3. Sandboxing & Versioning

* Nutze **VM2** oder Node’s **`vm.Module`** für isolierte Ausführung
* Vergleiche `manifest.apiVersion` mit deinem Core-API:

  ```ts
  if (manifest.apiVersion !== CORE_API_VERSION) {
    throw new Error(`Plugin ${name} expects API ${manifest.apiVersion}, core is ${CORE_API_VERSION}`);
  }
  ```
* Halte Versions-History in `.registry/plugins.json`:

  ```json
  {
    "poeticResonance": ["1.0.0","1.0.1","1.0.2"],
    "anotherPlugin": ["0.9.0"]
  }
  ```

